WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:02.728
(pensive music)

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.320
- [Narrator] India is battling

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.320
the world's fastest-growing surge

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.140
of COVID-19 cases.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.690
Hundreds of thousands of people

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.920
are testing positive each day

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.880
and likely, many more are falling ill.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.670
Now, the country is struggling

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.020
to make strides with vaccinations.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.950
- For months, they were
exporting tens of millions

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.360
of vaccines to other countries.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.450
Once numbers started going up,

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.450
the government essentially
halted almost all exports out

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.941
of India to reserve them for domestic use.

00:00:34.941 --> 00:00:37.920
- [Narrator] That crisis
is causing ripple effects

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.053
across the world.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.390
Here's why what is.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.840
India has a critical role

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.060
in global vaccination efforts.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.440
- India is not only a major
player in the global economy,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.780
it's also a major player

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.230
when it comes to global vaccines.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.260
And many of the plans to
vaccinate the developing world

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.230
were contingent upon India being able

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.610
to manufacture vaccine.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.560
- [Narrator] The Serum Institute of India,

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.000
the world's biggest vaccine maker,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.430
signed on to supply the shot
developed by AstraZeneca

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.220
and the University of Oxford

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.600
for an initiative backed

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.540
by the World Health
Organization, among others.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.070
The goal was to supply free vaccines

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.360
to 92 low and middle-income nations.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.610
After India largely stopped exporting

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.470
its coronavirus vaccines,

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.800
that initiative, called COVAX,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.500
was forced to slash the number

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.466
of shots it plans to
ship by the end of May.

00:01:28.466 --> 00:01:30.830
- We're gonna have the
entire world basically

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.500
on a delayed time scale for vaccination.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.170
- [Narrator] Roughly five
months into the vaccine rollout,

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.860
less than 4% of the world's population

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.460
is fully vaccinated

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.330
but doses haven't been distributed
evenly among countries,

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:48.690
a situation that threatens the
race to beat back the virus.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.060
In recent months,

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.530
countries from Indonesia to Rwanda

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.870
have had to re-jigger
their vaccine rollout,

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.310
with some countries
pausing their campaigns

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:59.250
and others looking elsewhere,

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.870
often to China, for supply.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.860
The Serum Institute doesn't
just supply vaccines

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.490
to the developing world.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:08.940
It has also filled orders
to developed countries,

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:09.893
like the UK.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.330
When manufacturing in
India will ramp enough

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:16.280
to meet demand is unclear.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.750
This is putting pressure
on Western governments

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.220
to support waiving vaccine patents

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.550
and on companies to supply millions

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.820
of doses to developing countries
as quickly as possible.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.010
Those vaccinations are crucial

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.960
to countries' abilities to manage

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.523
and minimize severe cases
and hospitalizations.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.210
- Basically, every single
hospital is overwhelmed.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.250
It doesn't matter where you are,

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.020
the infections are spreading
in rural India as well.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.700
It's everywhere and it's just burning

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.030
through the population.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.700
- I think it's very important to realize

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.563
that the situation in
India can happen anywhere.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.521
- [Narrator] With just over 2%

00:02:54.521 --> 00:02:59.030
of India's nearly 1.4 billion
people fully vaccinated,

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.750
a large percentage of the
population is still vulnerable.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.430
- Starting May 1st, everyone 18 and up,

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.970
so all adults, are eligible
to get the vaccine.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.570
That's some 900 million people.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:13.430
- [Narrator] And even with exports halted,

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.970
there aren't enough doses
to vaccinate everyone

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.030
who wants one.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.430
- They went from lopsided one-way

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.690
in that there was very little demand

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.150
and quite a lot of supply

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.840
to now a ton of demand

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.510
from people who are really scared

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.850
and think that vaccinations

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.171
are the only way to end this.

00:03:31.171 --> 00:03:33.970
The other kind of factor thrown in

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.380
that's probably an accelerant

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:40.080
to what would have already
been a surge are the variants.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.160
- [Narrator] A new
variant emerged in India

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.580
that has some concerning mutations,

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.200
one of which could make
it more contagious.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.040
The country is also grappling

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.890
with the more transmissible
variant from the UK.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.710
- When a more contagious variant arises

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:54.830
in a geographic area,

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.985
it means that you have to
get better at containing

00:03:56.985 --> 00:04:00.540
because this virus is
going to be less forgiving

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.650
when it comes to lapses in wearing masks,

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.770
lapses in hand washing,
lapses in social distancing.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:07.820
- [Narrator] Scientists
are still deciphering

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.430
what threats this new variant poses

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.700
to India and to other countries.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.650
The more any variant spreads,

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.400
the more opportunity
the virus has to mutate

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.500
and create additional variants.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.500
New variants could increase
the risk for reinfection

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.620
in people who were previously infected

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.640
with other versions of the virus

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.680
and available vaccines
could become less effective,

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.220
which could put a dent in global immunity.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.780
The key to ending this cycle

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.950
is increasing vaccination rates,

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.730
especially in the most
vulnerable populations.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.010
- [Amesh] The longer this pandemic rages,

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.630
even in one part of the globe,

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:46.470
the longer our lives
will be still not back

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:47.840
to our pre-pandemic status,

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.520
that the world is
interconnected, people travel.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.770
It has to be a priority

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.030
to fight this virus wherever it may be

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.770
if our goal is to return
to a pre-pandemic life

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.510
and to have as minimal disruption

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:00.028
from this virus as possible.

00:05:00.028 --> 00:05:02.778
(sirens ringing)

